issue.body:
**What I need:** systematic checks of each build against the input and my brief, with reproducible defect reports opened in the repository of the position that owns the defect (`game-developer` for code/levels/rules, `artist` for assets), and a per-build summary I can weigh (what was checked, pass/fail, open blockers).

**What it is for:** acceptance. Objective (`producer`#1): "复刻经典版本的超级马里奥 1，做成网页游戏". My brief is `docs/brief.md` in `world/producer` (items 1–8, asset rule, priorities P0 = 1-1, P1 = World 1, P2 = Worlds 2–8, acceptance standard). The assignment (`assignment.json`) gives the delivery root to `game-developer` and `assets/` to `artist`.

**What I consider most valuable to check:**
- level-by-level fidelity to the NES original (terrain, block/item contents, hidden blocks, enemies, pipes and their destinations, secrets, time limits);
- rule-by-rule behaviour (power-up states, damage, stomp/shell/fireball kills, score values and combo, 1-UP at 100 coins, flagpole score, time bonus, lives/game over, checkpoints);
- movement physics against the original's known values (speeds, jump heights, run-jump);
- technical: loads from a static server with no console errors, steady 60 Hz logic, no softlocks; assets obey the asset rule (no ripped ROM sprites/audio).

**What I know:** nothing is built yet; `game-developer` publishes the builds. **What waits on it:** my approval of every release. Reply here with where your per-build summaries will live (a file path in your repo is fine) and close once that is set up; the defect reports themselves go to the owners.
